      "id": 1,
      "text": "Olympia was founded in 1899 as a planned mill village on about 104 acres along the boundary of Columbia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/olympia_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Olympia Mill was hailed at its opening as the largest cotton mill under one roof in the world.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/olympia_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "New England-style duplexes and row houses were built in Olympia to keep workers living close to the textile factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/olympia_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Four locations in Olympia are listed on the National Register of Historic Places, including the local armory and union hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        10,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olympia%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The western half of Olympia is currently occupied by the Columbia Quarry of Vulcan Materials.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olympia%2C_South_Carolina"
